  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 92b2c8003586277498a007ee213cc22b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 'Log - [unassigned 4]'
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FloppyData
  diskName: 'Log - [unassigned 4]'
  logTitle: The Missing Interval
  author: '[Captain TBD]'
  shipName: '[Unassigned]'
  dateRecorded: '[TBD]'
  logText: 'Something peculiar happened with the ship''s clock yesterday.

    I
    finished cataloguing the surface samples at approximately 1400 hours. I remember
    checking the time because I was planning to eat afterward.

    The next time
    I looked, it was nearly 1700.

    Three hours.

    I don''t remember doing
    anything during that time. I hadn''t fallen asleep, at least not that I recall.
    I was still sitting at the same desk, with the same sample container in front
    of me.

    At first I thought the clock had simply jumped forward. But the
    computer''s activity records show several routine operations during those hours.

    Nothing
    unusual. Environmental checks, power distribution adjustments, a scheduled diagnostic.

    The
    records also indicate that I accessed the navigation terminal at 1532.

    I
    have no recollection of doing that.

    I checked the terminal. No course changes,
    no new destinations, nothing that would suggest I''d been working on anything
    important.

    Perhaps I was simply more tired than I realized.

    I''ve
    decided to keep a handwritten record of my activities for the next few days.
    If this happens again, I''d like to know whether the problem is with the computer
    or with me.'
